# {{lb|en|pharmaceutical drug}} An [[agent]] that [[prevent]]s or [[counteract]]s [[inflammation]].

====Usage notes====
* ''anti-inflammatory'' is several times more common than ''antiinflammatory'' in print.<ref>{{R:GNV|(antiinflammatory*3),anti-inflammatory}}</ref> GPO manual recommends using a hyphen to avoid doubling a vowel except after short prefixes.<ref>[https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GPO-STYLEMANUAL-2008/pdf/GPO-STYLEMANUAL-2008-8.pdf 6. Compounding Rules] in ''U.S. Government Printing Office Style Manual'', govinfo.gov</ref>

